        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThere are several way of using local plugins with 'mini.deps':\r\n- Put plugin along the others in target 'pack/deps/opt' directory and add it in the 'init.lua' with `add({ name = 'plugin-dir-name', checkout = 'HEAD' })`. For example, this is the way [I personally manage 'mini.nvim'](https://github.com/echasnovski/nvim/blob/4064584ccf637eb08f6fa5684302883123996101/init.lua#L31).\r\n- Have plugin into some directory and add it with `add({ source = '/full/path/to/plugin-dir-name', checkout = 'HEAD' })`.\r\n- Assuming it is local and doesn't require updating, manage it as any other plugin with built-in packages. For example, along the 'pack/deps' directory create 'pack/local' directory and put either 'start/plugin-dir-name' or 'opt/plugin-dir-name' (with later explicit `vim.cmd('packadd plugin-dir-name')`).\r\n\r\nNote that first two approaches require plugin to be a Git repository.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
