            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Hi @echasnovski\r\n\r\nthe second approach\r\n\r\n```\r\nHave plugin into some directory and add it with add({ name = '/full/path/to/plugin-dir-name', checkout = 'HEAD' })\r\n```\r\n\r\ndoesn't seem to work\r\n\r\nwith these lines:\r\n\r\n```\r\nMiniDeps.add({\r\n\tname = \"~/sync_git/nofrils\",\r\n\tcheckout = \"HEAD\",\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\ni got:\r\n\r\n```\r\nE5113: Error while calling lua chunk: (mini.deps) `name` in plugin spec should not contain \"/\".\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        [C]: in function 'error'\r\n        ...re/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.deps/lua/mini/deps.lua:1591: in function 'error'\r\n        ...re/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.deps/lua/mini/deps.lua:992: in function 'expand_spec'\r\n        ...re/nvim/site/pack/deps/start/mini.deps/lua/mini/deps.lua:475: in function 'add'\r\n        /home/aidan/.config/nvim/lua/nofrils.lua:3: in main chunk\r\n        [C]: in function 'require'\r\n        /home/aidan/sync_git/arch_config/.config/nvim/init.lua:53: in main chunk\r\n```\r\n\r\ni really don't want to put my local plugins into `~/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/deps/opt`",
