        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": ">     1. `source = \"~/abc/def\"` does not work, seems that tilde expansion is not supported, is this by design?\r\n\r\nIt is directly transferred to `git clone` without any changes. So if it doesn't support it, then 'mini.deps' (probably) won't either.\r\n \r\n>     2. `source = \"/home/aidan/abc/def\"` does work, but a warning message will appear when i run nvim for the first time:\r\n> \r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> (mini.deps) Warnings in `nofrils` during installing plugin\r\n> warning: --filter is ignored in local clones; use file:// instead.\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> do i need to make any adjustments?\r\n\r\nProbably, yes.\r\n \r\n>     3. `source = \"/home/aidan/abc/def\"` seems to clone the local repo to `~/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/deps/opt`, does mini.deps plan to provide an option to make the local repo the real plugin repo?\r\n\r\nYes, it will clone, because this is [how new plugin is ensured to be present](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c8922aef8207137e66c80acdb9523668599ba62a/doc/mini-deps.txt#L430). There will not be an option for treating local repo as the real plugin repo.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nUsing regular Vim packages (i.e. third option in original answer) is the suggested approach here. If you don't want to actually put it there, creating a symlink is also an option.",
